issue.body:
## Context

PR #67 added `checkAgeReviewDeadlines()` which handles:
- Slack alerts for cases approaching deadline (within 2 days, 12h dedupe)
- Auto-close of expired cases (state → `denied_closed`)

The function exists but is never called from the worker's `scheduled` handler in `worker/src/index.ts`.

## What to do

Add one call in the `scheduled` method (after the pre-auth nonce cleanup):

```typescript
// Age review deadline checks
try {
  await checkAgeReviewDeadlines(env);
} catch (error) {
  console.error('[scheduled] Failed to check age review deadlines:', error);
}
```

## Prerequisites

Wire this up once:
- `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` secret is set on staging/prod
- Cases are actually being created (mobile reports or moderator tooling)
- Keycast enforcement (Track C) is in place so auto-close has real consequences

## Related

- PR #67 — age review clock (defines the function)
- Track C (Keycast suspension) — without enforcement, auto-close is cosmetic

